Package: kpromm
Type: Package
Title: Mixed Minkowski-Metric Clustering with Statistical Normalization (k-PROMM / k-PROMMSA)
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Sofia", "Borodich Suarez", email = "sofia.borodich-suarez@neoma-bs.fr",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits k-PROMM and k-PROMMSA, clustering algorithms for mixed
    numerical/categorical data that combine a tunable Minkowski exponent p
    with statistical normalization of feature vectors, as originally
    developed in Suarez-Alvarez (2010, PhD thesis, Cardiff University) and
    Suarez-Alvarez, Pham, Prostov & Prostov (2012, Proceedings of the Royal
    Society A, 468(2145), 2630-2651). This package accompanies a manuscript
    that provides practical guidance for choosing p, benchmarks the method
    against established mixed-data clustering algorithms, and demonstrates
    it on a real decision-support application. kpromm() fits the algorithm
    at a single value of p (with normalization on by default, giving
    k-PROMMSA; off, giving unnormalized k-PROMM). screen_p() runs a
    labels-free ensemble screening procedure to narrow candidate values of p
    when ground-truth cluster labels are not available; consistent with the
    manuscript's honest evaluation of this procedure's limits, it does not
    auto-select a single p.
